  "changes": [
    "First machine uses the existing handle method for immediate prepare/validate/publish and checks the accepted outcome. Explicit scope, event identity, digest and logical time remain.",
    "machine::Digest reexports the existing task::Digest type; shared counter, timeline and durable examples use that same identity primitive. No hashing implementation, evaluator or identity generator added.",
    "Independent consumer build script extracts the canonical guide code fence, normalizes CRLF, and compiles it as first-machine. README runs it and stable/MSRV CI invokes it; no duplicate tutorial model.",
    "Facade package description includes typed state machines."
  ],
  "verified": {
    "compilers": [
      "1.100.0",
      "1.89.0"
    ],
    "canonical_guide": "Repository consumer and independent workspace with only the facade as a path dependency both print count = 3.",
    "public_branch": "Clean shallow Git clone and fresh cargo new / cargo add Git branch application both print count = 3 with both compilers; exact source SHA and generated dependency lock retained, no patches.",
    "core": "All-feature core tests plus no-default and serde bare-metal riscv32imafc profiles pass with both compilers.",
    "composition": "Timeline and durable consumer progressions pass with both compilers; strict all-target/all-feature consumer Clippy passes.",
    "regeneration": "An intentionally malformed guide changes the generated Rust compilation and exits 101; restoring the guide passes. CRLF copies run on both compilers.",
    "ci": "Pinned actions check and both workspace/consumer formatting checks pass. New stable/MSRV first-machine commands are committed; remote job success is not inferred from local runs."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The initial temporary verifier expected a mismatched-delimiter diagnostic, while rustc emitted unclosed-delimiter. Its expected compiler refusal succeeded, but its overly specific assertion aborted the driver. Failed output and script are retained; the corrected complete qualification and restoration pass.",
    "Core tests and composition checks precede the one-line CRLF extractor fix; their source hashes still match. The corrected extractor is independently checked with both compilers and from the final pushed Git checkout.",
    "CRLF tests execute on Linux; no native Windows or macOS execution claim.",
    "Scope/event/time metadata remains explicit. This does not claim an automatic local identity policy or zero-boilerplate API.",
    "Full final-source release CI, coverage, chaos, packages and open performance findings remain outstanding."
  ],
